    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs explorer",
      "text": "The WMRP contract contained a reentrancy vulnerability in its _removeLiquidity function, invoked during the transfer function. The contract failed to update its state before making external calls, allowing the attacker to repeatedly call the receive function via a malicious fallback function. This enabled the attacker to manipulate the transfer process, draining BNB by exploiting the lack of reentrancy guards and improper checks-effects-interactions pattern. Vulnerable code snippet: Attack tx: https://app.blocksec.com/explorer/tx/bsc/0x4353a6d37e95a0844f511f0ea9300ef3081130b24f0cf7a4bd1cae26ec393101 Analysis: https://blog.verichains.io/p/mrp-token-exploit-analysis"
    }
  ],
